The subsequent explosions, like the initial explosion, occupy a 3x3
square.  The center of each can be any of the 9 squares which was hit
by the initial explosion (the target square and the 8 squares
surrounding it).  Thus 9 squares is correct, and you can (in fact are
likely to) be hit at range 2.

Example:

.......
.......
.@.X...
.......
.......

@ = you; X = target square

Initial explosion:

.......
../-\..
.@| |..
..\-/..
.......

Subsequent explosion:

.......
./-\...
.| |...
.\-/...
.......

To be more precise:

.......
..123..
.@456..
..789..
.......

1-9 are possible centers of the subsequent explosions.  If an
explosion is centered at 1, 4, or 7 you will be hit by it.


